{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "units": [
    {
      "kind": "theorem",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.CenteredRootOrderInverse.actual_centered_root_order_inverse",
      "title": "Actual PBPS centered root order and bounded inverse",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A2",
          "label": "PBPS arXiv2609.06905v1 AppendixB15, genuine next B16 consumer; C2/C3/C4; exact original C2 and both Hessian bounds, eta cap; D1 real Hilbert order.",
          "scope": "Exact printed B15 centered positive-root order and internally derived bounded inverse on the SAME actual H_P^0, plus a genuine original-input Test showing normalized actual leakage preserves norm and lies in ker P. Full-joint inverse, completed polar map into the closed complement/onto claims, other B5, H1, B13/B14, event dynamics/nonexplosion/invariance/hypocoercivity/main mixing, implementation error, expected query costs and actual-input PBPS/SPHMC composition remain separate."
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        "lake build Tests.ProximalBPSCenteredRootOrderInverse"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "Finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel base E with canonical volume, including the disclosed rank-zero extension; V is C²; 0<α≤β; both global Hessian bounds; η>0 and βη≤1.",
        "Canonical normalized laws/kernel, onto pullback e, SAME U/T, full and centered roots, exact centering, gap, unit and bounded inverse are conclusions. Conditional actions are per-observable AE. L² is not assumed finite-dimensional.",
        "γ=2√(αη)/(1+αη); the inverse acts only on H_P^0=ker⟨e1,·⟩ with inherited Hilbert structure; the legal endpoint αη=1 is retained."
      ],
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X~μ and Z~N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J. These are probability laws. Put mY=comap(snd), H_P=L² classes measurable with respect to mY, P=i∘E[·|Y] and the canonical M:u↦u∘snd. Then H_P=ran(P), P is identity on H_P, and there exists an onto linear isometry e:L²(ν;ℝ)≃H_P with i e=M. There is a Markov kernel S whose every-state normalized law is S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)); Λ.IsCondKernel S and both Λ marginals equal ν. The same joint reflection F(x,y)=(x,2x−y) gives the involutive selfadjoint isometry U, with Uf=f∘F J-almost everywhere for every f. There is a bounded selfadjoint T on the full real L²(ν), with ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx) ν-almost everywhere for each u, and preserved integral. On H_P put A=PUP restricted via i and orthogonal projection, and B=(I_J−P)UPi:H_P→L²(J). Then A=eTe⁻¹ is selfadjoint and contractive, PB=0. There is a bounded positive operator Γ on the real scalar-valued L² space with Γ²=I−T². For the SAME transported Γ_P=eΓe⁻¹, positivity holds and Γ_P²=I_H_P−A²=B*B. There is q∈L²(ν;ℝ) equal to one ν-almost everywhere, with Tq=q and ⟨q,u⟩=∫u dν for every u. Set q_P=e q and H_P^0=ker⟨q_P,·⟩, with its inherited Hilbert structure. Membership is exactly zero ν-mean after e⁻¹. The SAME Γ_P annihilates q_P. Put γ=2√(αη)/(1+αη)>0. There exists Γ_0:H_P^0→H_P^0 equal under inclusion to the restriction of Γ_P, positive with Γ_0−γ I positive. Γ_0 is a unit in the algebra of bounded real operators. There exists a bounded real Inv on this SAME centered space with Inv Γ_0=Γ_0 Inv=I and ‖Inv‖≤1/γ. All probability, normalization, range, root, centering, spectral-gap, unit and inverse facts are internally derived from the original inputs; none is an additional public premise. αη=1 and rank-zero E remain legal. No inverse on full H_P is asserted.",
      "formula": "\\Gamma_0\\ge\\gamma I,\\quad\\gamma=\\frac{2\\sqrt{\\alpha\\eta}}{1+\\alpha\\eta}>0,\\quad\\mathrm{Inv}\\Gamma_0=\\Gamma_0\\mathrm{Inv}=I,\\quad\\|\\mathrm{Inv}\\|\\le\\gamma^{-1}.",
      "boundary": "Exact printed B15 centered positive-root order and internally derived bounded inverse on the SAME actual H_P^0, plus a genuine original-input Test showing normalized actual leakage preserves norm and lies in ker P. Full-joint inverse, completed polar map into the closed complement/onto claims, other B5, H1, B13/B14, event dynamics/nonexplosion/invariance/hypocoercivity/main mixing, implementation error, expected query costs and actual-input PBPS/SPHMC composition remain separate.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Keep the actual objects and identify the constant kernel",
          "text": "Reuse the exact accepted actual canonical laws, normalized kernel, reflection, macroscopic range and positive root. Mean preservation and selfadjointness yield T1=1. Transporting the accepted macro energy identity gives ‖Γu‖²=‖u‖²−‖Tu‖², so Γ1=0.",
          "formula": "Tq=q,\\quad \\langle q,u\\rangle=\\int u\\,d\\nu,\\quad \\|\\Gamma u\\|^2=\\|u\\|^2-\\|Tu\\|^2,\\quad\\Gamma q=0.",
          "lean": "  have hBase := MacroscopicDefectRoot.actual_unique_positive_macroscopic_defect_root\n      (E:=E) (V:=V) (α:=α) (β:=β) (η:=η) hα hαβ hV hH hη hβη\n  dsimp only at hBase\n  rcases hBase with\n    ⟨hμ,hJ,hν,hRange,hPf,S,hS,hSd,hSc,hSf,hSs,e,he,U,hU,hUi,hUs,\n      T,hTs,hAll,hAeq,hAs,hAn,hPB,Γ,hΓ,hΓSq,hΓP,hΓPSq,hGram,hEnergy,hUnique⟩\n  letI : IsProbabilityMeasure μ := hμ\n  letI : IsProbabilityMeasure J := hJ\n  letI : IsProbabilityMeasure ν := hν\n  let A : HP →L[ℝ] HP := HP.orthogonalProjectionOnto ∘L U.toContinuousLinearMap ∘L HP.subtypeL\n  let B : HP →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n    (((1 : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J)-P)*U.toContinuousLinearMap*P) ∘L HP.subtypeL\n  let ΓP : HP →L[ℝ] HP := e.conjStarAlgEquiv Γ\n  have hAeqLocal : A=e.conjStarAlgEquiv T := hAeq\n  let q : Lp ℝ 2 ν := AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.L2Expectation.one ν\n  have hq (u : Lp ℝ 2 ν) : inner ℝ q u=∫ y,u y ∂ν :=\n    AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.L2Expectation.inner_one_eq_integral ν u\n  have hqa : (q : E → ℝ)=ᵐ[ν] (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) :=\n    Lp.coeFn_const (α:=E) (μ:=ν) (p:=(2 : ℝ≥0∞)) (c:=(1 : ℝ))\n  have hTq : T q=q := by\n    apply ext_inner_right ℝ\n    intro u\n    calc\n      inner ℝ (T q) u=inner ℝ q (T u) := hTs.isSymmetric q u\n      _ = ∫ y,T u y ∂ν := hq _\n      _ = ∫ y,u y ∂ν := (hAll u).2.2\n      _ = inner ℝ q u := (hq _).symm\n  have hqq : inner ℝ q q=1 := by\n    rw [hq,integral_congr_ae hqa]\n    simp\n  have hΓEnergy (u : Lp ℝ 2 ν) : ‖Γ u‖^2=‖u‖^2-‖T u‖^2 := by\n    have hs := (hEnergy (e u)).2\n    have hAction : A (e u)=e (T u) := by\n      have hh : A (e u)=(e.conjStarAlgEquiv T) (e u) :=\n        congrArg (fun C : HP →L[ℝ] HP => C (e u)) hAeqLocal\n      exact hh.trans (by simp only [LinearIsometryEquiv.conjStarAlgEquiv_apply_apply,e.symm_apply_apply])\n    change ‖(e.conjStarAlgEquiv Γ) (e u)‖^2=‖e u‖^2-‖A (e u)‖^2 at hs\n    simpa only [LinearIsometryEquiv.conjStarAlgEquiv_apply_apply,e.symm_apply_apply,\n      hAction,e.norm_map] using hs\n  have hΓq : Γ q=0 := by\n    have h : ‖Γ q‖^2=0 := by rw [hΓEnergy,hTq,sub_self]\n    exact norm_eq_zero.mp (by nlinarith [norm_nonneg (Γ q)])\n",
          "detail": "Literal excerpt of the compiled declaration; preceding local definitions and proved facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/CenteredRootOrderInverse.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "3c4f72ef44868fe2ebca6842192ee4a9cea1db4527ae29dccdec691004e6daa6",
